------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <DataTableBulkBar> is a PURE presentational PRIMITIVE. Its inputs are plain props (count, onClear,
children, className) and it renders a selection toolbar. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO
Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or
disconnect from; its only "hook" is useTranslation, and the hosted bulk-action children own their own
states). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this
surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the accepted sibling
presentational primitives ActiveFilterChips (0147), InlineCallout (0124), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095),
and Accordion (0203) used. The REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • hidden              : count <= 0 → renders nothing (web `if (count <= 0) return null`).
  • visible + actions   : count label + the bulk-action slot (web `children`) + the clear button.
  • visible, no actions : count label + clear button only (never a blank box — count + clear always show).
  • polite announcement : the "{{count}} selected" live text (native peer of the count span
                          aria-live="polite"), posted on appear + on every visible count change, with a
                          rotating zero-width-space suffix so an identical consecutive count is re-read.
  • flex-wrap / Dynamic Type : the controls drop to their own line via ViewThatFits when width is tight.
Data source  : none (pure presentational; the selection count is a caller-supplied prop, not fetched).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : table.bulkActions.region ("Bulk actions"), table.bulkActions.selected ("{{count}}
               selected"), table.bulkActions.clear ("Clear selection") — all resolved through the P1/S10
               facade; no English literals in code.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "DataTableBulkBar" (P1/S11).
a11y         : the bar is one contained region labelled "Bulk actions"; the count text reads "{{count}}
               selected" and is re-announced politely on change; the clear button carries the explicit
               "Clear selection" label with its ✕ hidden from VoiceOver; the system focus engine supplies
               the keyboard focus ring (web focus-visible:ring-2); reduce-motion has no animation to gate;
               Dynamic Type via tokens + the wrapping fallback.

